-- Draft until reviewed by a cook from this tradition. No soaking needed; older beans just take longer.
Spread @dried black beans{500%g} on a #tray{} and pick out any small stones or shrivelled beans. Rinse them well in a #colander{}.

Put the beans in an #olla{} or other heavy pot with @water{2.5%l}, @white onion{1/2}, @garlic cloves{2} and @lard{1%tbsp}. Bring to a boil. ~{10%minutes}

Turn the heat down to the gentlest simmer and partly cover. Cook until the beans are soft and creamy inside. Check now and then: if the water dips below the beans, add hot water from a #kettle{}, never cold. ~{2%hours}

Taste a few beans. When they are completely tender, add @salt{2%tsp} and @epazote sprigs{2}. Simmer so the broth takes the flavour. ~{20%minutes}

Fish out the onion and the epazote stalks. Taste the broth and adjust the salt. Serve the beans in their broth in a #bowl{}, with warm @corn tortillas{6} on the side.
